/-!
# Main theorems of the curve-complex formalization

The four original declarations are available through this single entry module:

* Theorem 1.1 — `CurveComplexGenusTwo.SourceTopology.c1_contractible_genusTwo`:
  the entire C₁ realization is contractible for a genus-two surface.
* Theorem 1.2 — `CurveComplexGenusTwo.SourceTopology.c1_acyclic_genusTwo`:
  the entire C₁ realization is integrally acyclic for a genus-two surface.
* Theorem 1.3 — `CurveComplexGenusTwo.SourceTopology.c1_simplyConnected_allGenus`:
  the entire C₁ realization is simply connected in every genus at least two.
* Theorem 1.4 — `CurveComplex.HyperellipticModel.headline_hyperelliptic_dictionary`:
  the supplied genus-two hyperelliptic model gives the unique original
  arc/circle-to-essential-curve dictionary.

Each declaration retains its original hypotheses, statement, definitions, and
proof. Necessary proof sources live under `curve-complex/`.
-/
